						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">I don&#039;t think alot of the people complaining understand the scope of what really just happened.... This storm put a city of half a million people underwater... 80% of the city was submerged, in some cases by water 20 feet deep. <br /><br />There were far more people in the city for alot longer than anyone knew about. Once evacutations started another 20000 or more people appeared to jump on the busses.<br /><br />When disaster strikes, those who are smart enough, and motivated enough to take care of themselves will be alright. People who sit on thier asses bitching they want help are the cattle that get led to slaughter in a disaster. Sorry... that whole scene sickened me as an american. <br /><br />The do or die mentality in this country is only taken up by those who want to do better for themselves. We have given many people, not just black people either, this crosses all racial boundaries, because I see alot of white trash do it too, and expect a public welfare system to get them by. When people are offered a path of no or low resistance that allows them to simply get by, and not have to work a day in thier lives, many people will take it.<br /><br />Because by nature, alot of people are simply sheep.</td>
						</tr>
