						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">If this guy was taken seriously, then he&#039;d be quoted by the gaming mags everytime a new MMO comes out. I think his chart is a bunch of crap, I don&#039;t think Lineage has been that sucessfull, and by many reports FFXI did much better than he charts it.<br /><br />Again, it&#039;s all working off of rumors, and innuendo. And I don&#039;t buy for a minute that EQ2 is as sucessfull as he lists it. He&#039;s got it coming close to EQ1 subscriptions. <br /><br />I&#039;m not basing this just on EQ&#039;s numbered listing Lyhra, it&#039;s the sum of all his charting that looks suspect. <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1621.msg17778#msg17778">Quote from: Lhyra on July 28, 2005, 05:26:54 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1621.msg17777#msg17777">Quote from: Kinladar on July 28, 2005, 01:22:31 pm</a></div><div class="quote">the best he can do is guess.<br /></div><br />Ever take statistics?&nbsp; There is guessing...and there is educated guessing.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">My numbers come from a variety of sources, and some games have more than one source.&nbsp; These sources include the following:<br /><br />a)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Corporate Press Releases <br />b)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Corporate Documents <br />c)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;News <br />d)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Public Comments <br />e)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Anonymous Sources – Actually I do not have too many of these, although I certainly wish I had more.&nbsp; These are my own inside sources who are willing to give me numbers on the condition of anonymity.&nbsp; So far these have been pretty reliable – if their numbers are not exact, they are usually in the ballpark.&nbsp; As always, I have to use my best judgment in deciding whether or not a source is reliable.<br />f)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Educated Guesses – Very rarely, a number will appear on the chat that’s non-sourced and simply my educated guess based on known information.&nbsp; An example might be, “Well, we know they have at least 200K subscribers, and they’ve sold 600K copies, and their revenues are such-n-such, so I’m going to say they have at least 350K subscribers for the purposes of the chart.”&nbsp; I do not do this very often, and if I do, I’ll duly note it in the Analysis section by giving the data an appropriate Confidence Rating.<br /><br />It is true that many companies keep their subscriber numbers confidential, but others are more open about it.&nbsp; Almost all of the data I use comes from actual sources, although often those sources are insiders who only give the information on the condition of anonymity.&nbsp; If I simply wanted to make up numbers, I’d put out an update every week, and those updates would quickly be revealed as faulty when compared to, say, company press releases.&nbsp; So, while I am the first to admit that the data is not always reliable, it does represent the best research in the industry to date, and it is most definitely not made up – or at least, not by me.&nbsp; In the rare event that an actual “guess” does appear on my chart, you will find the Accuracy Rating for that MMOG appropriately adjusted my Analysis.&nbsp; For more discussion on this point, I recommend you read the Analysis section of my research and draw your own conclusions.</div></div></td>
